    <DataNode elementId="AT4G31940-MONOMER" textLabel="AT4G31940-MONOMER" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q9SZ46" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="300" centerY="215" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="THE-ARABIDOPSIS-INFORMATION-RESOURCE, zhang">|FRAME: AT4G31940 CYP82C4| was first described as a cytochrmoe P-450 that hydroxylates the furanocoumarin |FRAME: CPD-13042 xanthotoxin| at the 5 position. The activity was initially detected by screening 91 Arabidopsis seedlings overexpressing individual P450 enzymes against a panel of 50 compounds. To verify the activity, the gene was cloned and expressed in yeast. A related enzyme, encoded by the |FRAME: AT4G31970 CYP82C2| gene, also catalyzed the same activity |CITS: [18291319]|. The product, |FRAME: CPD-15055 5-hydroxyxanthotoxin|, is glycosylated in plants at the newly introduced hydroxyl group |CITS: [18291319]|. The enzyme was later shown to be involved in the production of |FRAME: CPD-21613 fraxetin| and |FRAME: CPD-21615 sideretin|, plant siderophores produced from |FRAME: SCOPOLETIN scopoletin|. |FRAME: AT4G31940 CYP82C4| was a strong candidate for the enzyme catalyzing the hydroxylation of |FRAME: CPD-21613 fraxetin| because its expression is upregulated by iron deficiency. Mutation of the gene resulted in disappearance of |FRAME: CPD-21615 sideretin| and accumulation of |FRAME: CPD-21613 fraxetin|. The gene was expressed in yeast, and incubation of the microsomal fraction with |FRAME: CPD-21613 fraxetin| and NADPH resulted in production of |FRAME: CPD-21614 sideretin (reduced form)| |CITS: [29581584]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT4G31940-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Araport" value="AT4G31940.1" />
