    <DataNode elementId="AT4G31970-MONOMER" textLabel="AT4G31970-MONOMER" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="O49394" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="450" centerY="215" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="THE-ARABIDOPSIS-INFORMATION-RESOURCE, zhang">The |FRAME: AT4G31970 CYP82C2| gene of |FRAME: TAX-3702 &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis thaliana&lt;/i&gt;|, which encodes a cytochrome P-450 enzyme, is highly expressed under a variety of pathogen treatment conditions. One of the enzyme&apos;s activities was found to be the hydroxylation of |FRAME: CPD-13042 xanthotoxin| to |FRAME: CPD-15055 5-hydroxyxanthotoxin| |CITS: [18291319]|. |FRAME: CPD-13042 Xanthotoxin| is a therapeutic furanocoumarin, or psoralen, that is primarily found in plants belonging to the Apiaceae and Rutaceae families. The product, |FRAME: CPD-15055 5-hydroxyxanthotoxin|, is glycosylated in plants at the newly introduced hydroxyl group|. The related Arabidopsis cytochrome P-P450 |FRAME: AT4G31940 CYP82C4| is also able to catalyze this activity |CITS: [18291319]|. A second activity is the 4-hydroxylation of |FRAME: CPD-21650 indole-3-carbonyl nitrile| to form |FRAME: CPD-21649 4-hydroxyindole-3-carbonyl nitrile| |CITS: [26352477]|. The &amp;alpha;-ketonitrile of these compounds is susceptible to nucleophilic attack, resulting in the displacement of a cyanide ion.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT4G31970-MONOMER" />
